※ pl4g-test: compile=error
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7015 LANG_MACRO_TOO_DEEP

※ What a macro writes is expanded in turn, so a macro may write another -- and one
※ that writes something reaching itself again would never finish.  Expansion is
※ stopped after a fixed number of rewrites, which is a limit rather than an
※ analysis: whether expansion ends is the halting problem.

macro endless:
    ⌜$x⌝ → ⌜endless⌜$x⌝⌝

@[startup]
fn main() → u6:
    ⎕narrow(endless⌜1u8⌝, ⌜u6⌝) ?? 1u6
